#: templates/premises/examples/contention.html:2
msgid ""
"The main contention. It will be arguable with own premises. The Premises can "
"prove or rebuttal this contention.<br> Examples: <ul> <li>Real art is for "
"society, not for profit</li> <li>The meaning of life is 42</li> <li>Ethics "
"man did what had to be done</li> </ul>"
msgstr ""
"其主要论点。其论述将是值得商榷的。\n"
"论述可以证明或反驳这一论点。<br>\n"
"例如：\n"
"<ul>\n"
"    <li>真正的艺术是为了社会，而不是以盈利为目的</li>\n"
"    <li>生命的意义就是 42</li>\n"
"    <li>道德的人做了必须做的事</li>\n"
"</ul>"

#: templates/premises/examples/fallacy.html:2
msgid ""
"You have to choose a fallacy type. For more information, you can look at the "
"<a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_fallacies\">wikipedia entry</"
"a> for fallacies."
msgstr ""
"你需要选择一个谬误类型。.\n"
"关于谬误的更多信息，你可以查看\n"
"<a href=\"https://zh.wikipedia.org/wiki/謬誤列表\">维基百科条目</a> 。"

#: templates/premises/examples/owner.html:2
msgid ""
"The owner of argument. It can be instutation, person, book, or a paper. "
"Examples: <ul> <li>On the Origin of Species</li> <li>Friedrich Nietzsche</"
"li> <li>Piet Mondiran</li> <li>The Guardian</li> </ul>"
msgstr ""
"论点的拥有者。它可以是一个机构，一个人，一本书，或者一篇文章。\n"
"\n"
"例如：\n"
"<ul>\n"
"    <li>物种起源</li>\n"
"    <li>尼采</li>\n"
"    <li>蒙德里安</li>\n"
"    <li>卫报</li>\n"
"</ul>"

#: templates/premises/examples/premise.html:2
msgid ""
"Example: We define happiness as a state of well-being, starting with being "
"alive instead of dead."
msgstr "例如：我们定义幸福是一种好的状态，前提是 活着而不是死亡。"

#: templates/premises/examples/premise_source.html:2
msgid "Example: Charles Darwin's The Origin of Species"
msgstr "例如：查尔斯·达尔文的物种起源"

#: templates/premises/examples/premise_type.html:3
msgid ""
"The type of premise. It can be: <ul> <li> but: An objection against the "
"contention. </li> <li> because: A reason for proof the contention. </li> "
"<li> however: An additional situation for the premise. </li> </ul>"
msgstr ""
"论述的类型。它可以是：\n"
"<ul>\n"
"    <li>\n"
"        但是：对争论的反对。\n"
"    </li>\n"
"    <li>\n"
"        因为：对争论的支持。\n"
"    </li>\n"
"    <li>\n"
"        然而：论述的另外一个条件。\n"
"    </li>\n"
"</ul>"

#: templates/premises/examples/sources.html:2
msgid ""
"The source of argument. It can be a URL, a book, or a newspaper. It is "
"important for reliability of main contention."
msgstr ""
"论点来源。它可以是一个网址，一本书，或一张报纸。\n"
"它对主要论证的可靠性很重要。"

